    "title": "Motorcyclist critically injured in south Austin crash - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Ethan Love ,\n5 hours ago\nAUSTIN (KXAN) – A motorcyclist was critically injured in a single-vehicle crash Wednesday afternoon in south Austin, according to Austin-Travis County Emergency Medical Services.\nThe collision was reported about 5:04 p.m. in the 5100 block of Ponciana Drive. That’s near Interstate 35 and Teri Road.\nATCEMS arrived to find an adult patient in critical condition and initiated CPR upon arrival, the agency said.\nThe patient was later taken to St. David’s South Austin Medical Center with life-threatening injuries. No additional details about the crash or the patient’s condition have been released.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to KXAN Austin.",
